LG V60 IMS: extend the strongSwan `stroke` wire ABI to match LG's charon.

LG's V60 `charon` expects extra trailing fields on `stroke_end_t` (recovered from
the config-token order in LG's `starter` binary and confirmed by charon's own
`invalid stroke message length` on a bare-upstream client). Apply against a clean
strongSwan 5.7.1 tree, then build only the `stroke` binary for aarch64 with the
Android NDK and install it at /system_ext/bin/stroke.

Types are best-effort: all `char *` except `svn` (a small integer, seen live as
`leftsvn=24`). Field order matches LG's insertion order
(pcscf / imei / sourceif / intnetmask / intsubnet cluster, then idr_apn, then svn).

--- a/src/stroke/stroke_msg.h
+++ b/src/stroke/stroke_msg.h
@@ -166,6 +166,15 @@ struct stroke_end_t {
 	uint8_t protocol;
 	uint16_t from_port;
 	uint16_t to_port;
+
+	/* LG IMS extensions (V60) - appended block, see patch header */
+	char *pcscf;
+	char *imei;
+	char *sourceif;
+	char *intnetmask;
+	char *intsubnet;
+	char *idr_apn;
+	int svn;
 };

 typedef struct stroke_msg_t stroke_msg_t;
